{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116696","id":3318234519,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7FyD2X","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116696","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116696.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116696.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116696","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116696/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116696/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116696/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/54c26bb93d094713f5ad1ce3e2f3db1b01a436fe","number":116696,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix GLSL shader include","user":{"login":"sblana","id":146403816,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLnx6A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146403816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana","html_url":"https://github.com/sblana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sblana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #80532 by implementing the `Includer` interface from glslang. Note that includes via `ShaderIncludeDB` should not be affected by this PR.\r\nLocal-style (`\"path\"`) and system-style (`<path>`) includes are treated the same.\r\nAn inclusion extension (`GL_ARB_shading_language_include` or `GL_GOOGLE_include_directive`) needs to be enabled to be able to include files. This matches standard GLSL behaviour, but is a breaking change.¹ The Godot editor displays a helpful glslang error however.\r\nI've set an arbitrary depth limit of 1000 to prevent cyclic includes from freezing the engine indefinitely. Should this be something like a project setting instead?\r\n\r\n[Here](https://github.com/sblana/Godot-GLSL-include-tests) is a repo with some test cases.\r\n\r\n¹ The breaking change is this:\r\nCurrently\r\n```glsl\r\n#[compute]\r\n#version 460\r\n#include \"include_a.glsl\"\r\n...\r\n```\r\nAfter this PR\r\n```glsl\r\n#[compute]\r\n#version 460\r\n#extension GL_ARB_shading_language_include : enable // or require,\r\n// which in this case does the same thing.\r\n// GL_GOOGLE_include_directive can also be used instead.\r\n#include \"include_a.glsl\"\r\n...\r\n```\r\nNote that this _is_ expected and correct behaviour according to GLSL spec ([see §3.3 of GLSL 4.6 spec](<https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL/specs/gl/GLSLangSpec.4.60.pdf#preprocessor>)). It may be unintuitive to people using GLSL for the first time, so perhaps this should be mentioned in the docs?","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milesto